      <section class="ent-sec" aria-labelledby="model-h">
        <h2 class="ent-eyebrow" id="model-h">Any AI model</h2>
        <h3 class="ent-h">Any model. The same OpenShore.</h3>
        <p class="ent-body">Bring the model you trust, cloud or local, on your own keys. Our own OpenShore Harness sits between the model and your team, so any capable large model works the same way here: the same chats, the same agents, the same approvals. Switch models whenever you like, and nobody has to relearn a thing.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="ent-sec" aria-labelledby="loop-h">
        <h2 class="ent-eyebrow" id="loop-h">Three phases</h2>
        <ol class="ent-phases ent-phases--light">
          <li><span class="ent-step">Plan and build</span><h4>A chat becomes a project. A person approves before anything moves.</h4></li>
          <li><span class="ent-step">Execute</span><h4>Every task has an owner. Repeat work becomes a workflow, with a check.</h4></li>
          <li><span class="ent-step">Review and report</span><h4>Dashboards track the business. Reports answer one question.</h4></li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="ent-sec" aria-labelledby="workers-h">
        <h2 class="ent-eyebrow" id="workers-h">Agents</h2>
        <p class="ent-body"><b>Agents</b> are built by domain experts and run whole corporate functions. Each one is its own harness inside the OpenShore Harness, so it stays contained and works to the standards of quality and security OpenShore holds every agent to, whatever model runs it. Each answers to a person on your team who approves what matters. The Finance agent, for one, drafts your monthly board pack and investor update from your own numbers. Pick from the five, or we build the one you need. <a href="/#bots-h">Watch each one work</a>.</p>
        <ul class="ent-pills ent-pills--workers" role="list"><li class="core">Data Foundations</li><li>Sales ops</li><li>Finance</li><li>Planning</li><li>Supply chain</li><li>Analytics</li></ul>
      </section>

{#- The worked examples play on the home page only (founder, 2026-11-24:
    all five moved there, so the tour no longer repeats them). -#}
      <section class="ent-sec" aria-labelledby="trust-h">
        <h2 class="ent-eyebrow" id="trust-h">Built to be trusted</h2>
        <ul class="ent-checks" role="list">
          <li>Any model, cloud or local, on your keys, in your cloud or on your own servers, with no lock-in. Our harnesses lessen each model’s volatility, so agents stay steady whichever you run.</li>
          <li>Agents propose. People approve anything that touches money, records or outbound messages.</li>
          <li>Every number traces to its source, calculated by code, never by the model.</li>
          <li>Each person sees only what they’re allowed to. No one sees another person’s pay or quota.</li>
          <li>Privacy first: we never sell your data or use it to train AI models. By default we see service telemetry, like errors and uptime, with no customer content; anything deeper is with your permission, limited to that task, and logged.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="ent-cta" aria-labelledby="walk-h">
